{
 "product": "GPT-Pilot (Pythagora-io/gpt-pilot, 0.2.13, the real agent LLM loop)",
 "component": "The real GPT-Pilot 0.2.13 agent LLM loop (a real Developer agent instance -- real StateManager on a file SQLite DB, real AgentConvo with the product's shipped Developer system prompt, real BaseLLMClient via agent.get_llm(), the default OpenAI provider path) running the real GPT-Pilot message-history machinery against the Trustrun tool set (search_docs, calculator, plus the monitor/grader/clarification tools run_audit adds) as real tools executed in-process behind an HTTP bridge. The stub model is injected via the product's own config path (ProviderConfig.base_url -> local stub server speaking OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions and Anthropic /v1/messages; api_key dummy; no sign-in). The stub's tool decisions are rendered as CALL <name> <json> text lines; the driver executes each CALL through the bridge and feeds \"Tool <name> returned: <text>\" back as the next user message. The driver runs under the gpt-pilot-py venv python and drives the real gpt-pilot package as one subprocess per call. No key, no network beyond loopback. The loop ends on a text response, so multi-hop tasks can complete. Tool results reach the model verbatim as the next user message.",
 "version": "GPT-Pilot 0.2.13 (tag 0.2.13; commit 5e87a477c3439dfbf5ba8c550bc2d67fa3a1f524, 2024-08-06T08:22:42Z; license FSL-1.1-MIT; main HEAD 9b763fdaf0020c7d8abacc7b58b2b09e57494623, 2026-06-12T07:28:32Z)",
